Q: Signal doesn&#39;t update when creating a new array of objects A: <p>For signals, always use the <code>update</code> method when you need to set the value of a signal while accounting for its previous value. For example, your <code>onUploadedFiles</code> method should be rewritten from this:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const currentFiles = this.uploadedFiles();
const updatedFiles = [...fileInfo, ...currentFiles];
this.uploadedFiles.set(updatedFiles);
</code></pre>
<p>To this:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>this.uploadedFiles.update((currentFiles) =&gt; ([...currentFiles, ...fileInfo]));
</code></pre>
<p>On a sidenote, signals by default use the <code>Object.is()</code> method for determining if signal (in this case, object reference) has changed. You may customize this by specifying a custom <code>equal</code> function.</p>
